    ---
    
    **CLASSIFICATION: AURORA-RESTRICTED / ASSESSOR TIER III AND ABOVE**
    **DATE: Cycle 7, Long-Light Quarter, Year of the Settled Fracture**
    **UNIT: E'frostlings Commercial Reconnaissance Detail, 4th Terrace Bureau**
    **SUBMITTED TO: Senior Assessor Angmo xang'Oath, E'frostlings Central Holdings**
    **PREPARED BY: Qingchaifoxa (beacon-lit) Molok'Arch, Field Assessor, 4th Bureau**
    
    ---
    
    **MISSION & STATUS**
    
    We were tasked with asset-exposure profiling of Collective☽ Of Led∴merch commercial infrastructure along the Nightshelf mid-tunnel corridor, with emphasis on resource throughput at contested extraction site ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~ and proliferation status of proprietary capabilities. Detail is intact. One member reassigned to courier-channel observation at Midway Shelf, duration open-ended.
    
    ---
    
    **OBSERVATIONS**
    
    Collective☽ Of Led∴merch maintains operational control of ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~ but extraction output has declined an estimated 31% since last verified count. We observed fourteen active mining crews across three shifts—down from twenty-two per [INTERCEPTED GUILD-MINUTES, source: ☽'fluxus, reliability grade B+]. Fire-core yield at the site remains extraordinary: Class III units at double standard burn-time, Class IV purple-spectrum product sourced exclusively from the deep seams. However, the corruption spreading from The Forgotten Shore has reached the secondary chamber where the Thron∴mbra Fracta split the stone. Miners working below the breach line are rotating out at accelerated intervals. We counted six with visible cold-burn discoloration on exposed flipper-joints. The ash trace-signature on extracted cores now triggers resonance readings at forty burns rather than the previously documented threshold. This is an unpriced liability. We note it because someone must.
    
    The Covens' off-ledger logistics—the ledger that leaves no ledger—still bypass Courier Corps channels through at least three tunnel routes we have confirmed and two we suspect. Estimated volume moving outside Accord-sanctioned trade: 60-65% of total Coven commerce. Official courier manifests show Coven-stamped crates down to nine per cycle at Midway Shelf. [FULL MANIFEST DATA RESTRICTED — TIER IV CLEARANCE REQUIRED.]
    
    Star∴eternal deployment observed in two sentries at the Umbra's eastern access. Bone-lattice conduits visible through translucent flipper structure. These operators detected our detail at approximately 400 body-lengths—pressure-depth perception through ice. The technology's surveillance range exceeds our previous estimates by a factor we find professionally uncomfortable. Fire-feeding requirement noted: each operator consumed one Class II core per half-shift. A supply chain that never sleeps is a supply chain that can be starved, but someone has to be willing to starve it.
    
    ---
    
    **ENCOUNTERS**
    
    We were contacted at the Thrall☽ Vavmastius corridor junction by Void-Merchant Liaselis-obscur~, identifying herself as guild-escorted passage coordinator. She offered tripartite certification services—☽'tenebris's triple-mark seal—unprompted. Current rate quoted: forty-three aurora-shards per Class II unit. We declined. She did not press. She did note, with the careful neutrality of someone rehearsing a message, that the Shadow Parliament has not convened in full quorum for two cycles. "Restructuring," she called it. We have attended more productive funerals.
    
    ---
    
    **TACTICAL ASSESSMENT**
    
    The Collective is a firm in managed decline. Their moat—shadow logistics, off-ledger trade, operational secrecy—remains intact but is shrinking around a contracting resource base. The fire-core supply crisis compresses their entire model. ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~ is their last high-yield asset, and it is corrupting faster than they are extracting. Star∴eternal gives them surveillance dominance we cannot replicate. The Swaleed~ Luminary still authenticates the Pactum∴silenti—fire you can't afford to keep or let go dark. Its destruction would void their commercial charter entirely. No one has proposed this. The market share no one claims aloud hangs on a glass vessel scarred by three wars.
    
    Post-Frost-heir, we know what institutional collapse looks like. We are still calculating the exposure.
    
    ---
    
    **RECOMMENDATIONS**
    
    1. Increase courier-channel monitoring at Midway Shelf to quantify exact off-ledger volume differential. 
    2. Commission burn-threshold study on corrupted Class III cores before any acquisition consideration.
    3. Map Star∴eternal fire-core consumption rates against Coven supply projections. The vulnerability is logistical, not tactical.
    4. Do not acquire ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~. Not yet. Let them carry the cost of what's spreading.
    
    ---
    
    **[END REPORT — DO NOT CIRCULATE BELOW TIER III — FILE IN CIPHER]**
  CANONICAL_CHRONICLE
  annotation "note_1771582069833_0", anchor: "pressure-depth perception through ice", text: "The modern reader may not register that this single report inventories all three sources of Berg magic as commercial data: fire-cores (captured fire), aurora-shards (aurora-light), and Star∴eternal's pressure-depth perception. The complete magical taxonomy of penguin civilization, reduced to logistics. Qingchaifoxa has catalogued the foundational framework of her world's power without recognizing she has done so. The Clever Ice Age in miniature — mastery so total it forgets it is mastery.", type: :pedantic, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582069833_1", anchor: "Post-Frost-heir, we know what institutional collapse looks like", text: "They know what collapse looks like, and they are calculating commercial exposure against a shadow guild's shrinking fire-core yield. They are not calculating the orca war-pods massing beyond the outer currents — intelligence every Nightshelf whisper-channel was carrying by this date. An entire reconnaissance detail in the mid-tunnels, intercepted guild-minutes in flipper, and not one word about the thing that will make every number in this report irrelevant. The E'frostlings always had a gift for cataloguing the wrong apocalypse with immaculate precision.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582069833_2", anchor: "Estimated volume moving outside Accord-sanctioned trade: 60-65%", text: "A professionally comfortable range estimate from a detail that could not enter Coven territory without being detected at four hundred body-lengths. The precision here is decorative.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
